MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_001: The structure is fascinating... The stalk is thick,\nsupporting large, veined leaves...
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_002: Did you draw that yourself? It's pretty good!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_003: Ah. Another creature devoid of tact. Tell me, what\nbrings you out here?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_004: I'm on break. Thought I'd come out here for a snack.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_005: A snack? You can't mean these weeds.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_006: You got it. These flowers got good nectar, and the\nbeans are best straight off the vine!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_007: I see. You were eating wild plants. I apologize for any\noffense. The people of Saramis are singular indeed.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_008: Since setting foot on Dagdan soil, I have been, and\ncontinue to be, amazed by what I find.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_009: Wanna munch on some leaves with me, Fabi?\nYou'd like 'em!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_010: Thank you, but no.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_011: As far as caloric intake, there are more palatable\noptions. I am here to sketch, and sketch I shall.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_012: Huh. You'd rather draw than eat? In that case...
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_013: I'm gonna round up a few plants—some good, some\npoison. You mind drawing 'em for me?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_014: I fail to see how that would benefit me, or why\nyou would ask it.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_015: The pictures will help folks tell 'em apart. Wouldn't\nwant anyone mixing 'em up, you know?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_016: Might as well do some good while you're drawing,\nsince it's your hobby anyway.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_017: I'll be right back. Till then, why don't you get started\ndrawing the glirmosa growing over there?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_018: But don't eat it! One lick and you'll be out cold for\nthree solid days.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_019: {SetColor=Gray}And off he charges through the brush, brutish and\nheedless—a perfect beast.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_020: {SetColor=Gray}Protest any more and I can see I will only become\nvexed. I will satisfy him with some simple sketches.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_021: I brought a whole pile for you. Hey, look at that!\nYou already finished one!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_022: Yes, the glirmosa, and only the glirmosa, so far. If\nthis is intended as a reference, I'll add the name...
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_023: No need for that. The picture's plenty. Thanks!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_024: Ah, I see. You cannot read. That is not so surprising,\nI suppose—your lack of interest in the written word.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_025: Eh...you're right that I can't read. But that's just\n'cause of our kingdom's laws.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_026: See, way back when, our goddess said written words\nwere bad. So we don't use 'em.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_027: Ah, yes. It seems I must apologize once again.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_028: Hey, no skin off my nose! Anyway, here's what\nI got for you.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_029: These ones are safe to eat, so keep those drawings\nseparate! When you're done, you can chow down.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_030: Unlike you, I do not graze upon weeds.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_031: These plants are more numerous than anticipated. It\nmay take me some time.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_032: Hehehe! Sorry about that. Good of you to do\nit anyway!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_C_033: {SetColor=Gray}Ahh... This man is another the gods have\nstolen from.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_001: Here—your sketches. Do they suffice?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_002: Wow! A whole stack of these, and they're all real\nas life. You're a pro at this!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_003: It does pain me to omit the names of the specimens...\nBut I suppose this is fine work done for free.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_004: Guess I oughta treat you to some nice wine to\nsweeten the deal. No hard feelings then! Heh heh!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_005: Tell me... Do you not hate your goddess?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_006: Heheh— Huh? Where's this coming from?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_007: You have lived a long life without reading...\nWithout study.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_008: If the written word had not been stolen from you,\nyour life might be very different.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_009: Never thought about that before. Probably not\ngonna start now.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_010: Perhaps this very restriction—this prohibition on\nwriting—impedes your ability to reason.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_011: Now hold on there, Fabi! Don't go thinking we\nSaraminians are idiots.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_012: We've known what's what since waaay back, even\nbefore my grandpa's grandpa was still kicking!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_013: Saramis doesn't need writing to be the best there is\nat making war and sailing ships!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_014: I wondered what you might offer as a rejoinder.\nWriting or no, your kingdom will endure, yes.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_015: But I am not asking of your kingdom—I know well\nthat society can exist without writing. I ask of you.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_016: From the moment of your birth, your goddess has\ndeprived you of the choice to learn the written word.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_017: Choice, huh? Well, look at it this way.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_018: Instead of an axe, you hold a pen. Your life's about\nsitting around and making sense of weird patterns.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_019: Can you really see a guy like me living that life?\nBaw haw haw...
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_020: I sense some bias against writing itself in your words.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_021: Even if you're right...I've lived a long time by now.\nWhy look back on what mighta been?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_022: Yes, a long life of 50 years. How remarkable.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_023: Your life is so short, so fleeting... Yet it seems that\nyour conclusions are all the stronger for it.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_024: Huh? You saying I'm young? Young at heart,\nthat's for sure!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_025: I don't let the new blood in their teens and twenties\nshow me up, and you shouldn't either, Fabi!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_B_026: Oh, indeed not.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_001: Hey there, Fabi! Wanna knock back some wine\nwith me?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_002: Oh? What a surprise. Till now, you have asked for\nfavors and offered none.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_003: I told you I'd treat you to the good stuff in exchange\nfor those pictures! Unless you're not a wine guy.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_004: I do not dislike it. I am not, however, in the habit\nof partaking.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_005: As Dietrich despises the stuff, it has been some time\nsince I had the chance, now that I consider it.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_006: Then you're gonna flip for what I've got for you!\nC'mon, we're going out.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_007: Ohhh. That is one gorgeous-looking moon! And just\nfeel that night breeze.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_008: I see. You enjoy gazing at the moon when you're in\nyour cups.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_009: *glug* *glug* Ahhhh! This is the life!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_010: Hm.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_011: {SetColor=Gray}Were I to have lived like this man, pure and\noblivious...what would have become of me?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_012: {SetColor=Gray}Would I have been able to lead a fleeting, vivid life,\nlike a beast?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_013: What's wrong, Fabi? You ain't so much as had a sip.\nDon't hold back! Drink up!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_014: Oh, I have no intention to abstain. I was lost\nin contemplation.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_015: For your part, you may have drunk too much already.\nDrink too much and you may well die young.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_016: You worried? That's real sweet of you. But when it's\nmy time to go, I want it to involve wine!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_017: Is that so? If your impulse is toward self-destruction,\nthen so be it.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_018: Hehehe! You're a swell guy, Fabi. And so is this\nwine! Here's to chance encounters!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_019: *glug* *glug* Ahhhh!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_020: Encounters, you say? I had a fateful one.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_021: I spent so long in the dark... Moving from vessel to \nvessel to vessel... And then I encountered him.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_022: Heh. Didn't you once suggest that you knew only\none way to live, and no other?
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_023: Eh? Don't tell me you're a booze philosopher before\nyou get started drinking.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_024: It is nothing. *gulp*
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_025: Attaboy! And I bet you're just getting started.\nThe night's still young!
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_026: Yes. I reached the conclusion that enjoying a dram\nunder the moon's tranquil light is no bad thing.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_027: Tobias, may I trouble you for your company for a bit\nlonger? Today, at least, I would share a drink or two.
MID_SE_Fab_Tob_A_028: Baw haw haw! Like you gotta ask! I could drink\nfrom here till sunrise!